# Input
```ts
/* should generate diagnostics */
function a(value: string) { value.trim().endsWith("-"); }
function b(value: string) { value.trim().startsWith("-" as const); }
function c(value: string) { value.trim().endsWith("-" satisfies string); }
(value as string).trim().startsWith("-");
value!.trim().startsWith("-");
{ const prefix = "foo" as const; value.trim().startsWith(prefix); }

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.ts:2:35 lint/nursery/noUnnecessaryStringTrim  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i This trim() call removes whitespace from both ends of the string, but endsWith() only needs it removed from the end.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ function a(value: string) { value.trim().endsWith("-"); }
      │                                   ^^^^^^
    3 │ function b(value: string) { value.trim().startsWith("-" as const); }
    4 │ function c(value: string) { value.trim().endsWith("-" satisfies string); }
  
  i Whitespace at the start of the string can't change the result of endsWith() here.
  
  i Use trimEnd() to remove whitespace from the end only.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Use trimEnd() instead.
  
